  "term": "anabolic-androgenic steroid",
  "definition": "Anabolic-androgenic steroid (AAS) is a substance whose use can be linked to dependence and craving in some people. In the mental health context, the term often appears when discussing problematic AAS use and efforts to measure AAS dependence and craving.",
